cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this artifact, please cite it as below."
title: "Open Knowledge Format v0.2 as a Retrieval Substrate: A Controlled Evaluation Across Five RAG Pipelines"
abstract: >-
  A controlled, paired evaluation of one pinned Open Knowledge Format (OKF) v0.2
  producer and two disclosed consumers inside five unchanged retrieval-augmented
  generation pipelines, on a single regulatory document with a 93-question
  benchmark. The confirmatory comparison against ordinary vector retrieval is a
  null. A diagnostic decomposition shows that the large advantage initially
  observed for the lexical OKF consumer is attributable to lexical matching and
  to a dense baseline whose encoder truncated most of each passage, not to the
  format; plain BM25 with no OKF component scores higher still. The artifact
  contains the producer, consumers, bundle, questions, answer keys, all raw model
  outputs, and the analysis and manuscript generation code.
type: software
version: "0.1.0"
